.TH KB_SET_EXPORTED_OUTPUTS 2 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
KB_SET_EXPORTED_OUTPUTS \- Set all outputs marked as "exported" with the
piControl driver

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.B "#include <sys/ioctl.h>"
.sp
.BI "int ioctl(int " fd ", KB_SET_EXPORTED_OUTPUTS, const void *" process_image ");"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
Write all variables marked as "exported" in the same cycle.

It is possible to mark output variables as "exported" in the configuration
file, which enables this
.BR ioctl (2)
to write all of them in the same cycle.

This
.BR ioctl (2)
takes a pointer
.I process_image
to a modified copy of the entire process image as the only
argument. The output values in the process image can be changed by the user
before calling this
.BR ioctl (2),
which then modifies all the outputs marked as "exported" in the same cycle.

It is guaranteed that all outputs will be written in the same cycle.

If no outputs are marked as "exported" in the configuration, the call to
.B KB_SET_EXPORTED_OUTPUTS
is a no-op.

.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.

On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.

.SH ERRORS
Error codes set in
.I errno
can be, among others, one of the following:
.TP
.B EAGAIN
A driver reset is in progress.
.TP
.B EINVAL
The parameter
.I process_image
is invalid.
.TP
.B EFAULT
Failure on copying values to/from caller.

.SH CAVEATS

As it is currently implemented this
.BR ioctl (2)
should only be called by one application at a time.

.SH EXAMPLES

.EX
unsigned char process_image[4096];
/* read full process image into modifiable buffer */
read(fd, process_image, 4096);
/* change output values in the copy of the process image */
// \.\.\.
/* pass modified process image to piControl to write new output values */
if (ioctl(fd, KB_SET_EXPORTED_OUTPUTS, process_image) < 0)
	perror("Setting exported outputs");
.EE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioctl (2),
.BR piControl (4)
